   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 506 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax in the town of North Castle, in relation\nto extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8040",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8040-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 506 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8040\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 506 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of an occupancy tax in the town of North\nCastle, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend by 3 years the authorization for\nthe Town of North Castle to have a room occupancy tax not to exceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 extends from September 1, 2022 to September 1, 2025 the\nauthorization for the Town of North Castle to have a room occupancy tax.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of North Castle seeks the continued authority to impose a 3%\ndaily room tax on any room in a hotel, motel, or similar place. This tax\nraises revenues to support municipal expenses, particularly the repave-\nment of local roads. The tax has been successful in the neighboring\nmunicipalities of Harrison, Rye Brook and White Plains.  Chapter 506 of\nthe Laws of 2016 grants the authority to the Town of North Castle; this\nbill would extend the expiration date.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: Chap. 204\n\n2016: Chap. 506\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State, but increased revenue for the Town of North Castle.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed September 1, 2025.\n",
